Empty the GamePak prefetch buffer on every PC write: the runtime's half.

The GamePak prefetch model (rwt_prefetch_stall, "exactly mGBA
GBAMemoryStall") keeps the buffer's position in
RuntimeWaitTable::last_prefetched_pc, and nothing but a reset or a state
load cleared it. mGBA clears it on every PC write (GBASetActiveRegion sets
lastPrefetchedPc = 0, called by ARMWritePC; mGBA 0.10.5 src/gba/memory.c:273,
the same in 1d201b22). Without the reset, a loop that runs from the
cartridge and stores to RAM kept the position of the opcodes after the
loop across its branch back, and its store cost 8 cycles instead of 4: with
WAITCNT 0x4317, `cmp r1, r2; strcc r3, [r1], #4; bcc` took 26 cycles per
iteration instead of mGBA's 22.

arm-recomp-core's half (0001-prefetch-reset-on-pc-write.patch of the
arm-recomp-core series in the same repository as this patch) adds
Bus::prefetch_reset, calls it from Interpreter::step after any PC write,
and resets the position after the refill of every direct branch in
generated code. This patch:

- GbaBus::prefetch_reset clears its wait table's position (gba_bus.h); the
  force-interp backend's bus adapter forwards it (ForceInterpBus,
  runtime_arm_default_aborts.cpp), like prefetch_stall. The self-heal
  bridge steps the GbaBus directly.
- runtime_refill_cycles, which generated code charges for every PC write
  known only at run time (BX, LDR/LDM/POP to PC, data-processing writes to
  PC, exception returns through runtime_exception_return_refill), clears
  it too (runtime_wait_inline.h, shared with the Stage-2 overlay shim).
- The widescreen sidecar's shadow draws run guest code whose PC writes now
  clear the live position; it saves and restores it with the rest of the
  state it restores (ws_sidecar.cpp). Stalls in shadow mode already
  evaluate on a copy (runtime_prefetch_stall_delta).
- codegen_tests' bus forwards the reset to the table the generated side
  reads, so the per-instruction comparison of the buffer position covers it
  (tests/codegen/test_main.cpp).
- interpreter_smoke checks that the interpreter resets the buffer once
  after each kind of PC write and never otherwise
  (tests/armv4t/interpreter_smoke.cpp).
- docs/CPU_TIMING.md describes the reset.

SWI entry does not reset it: the BIOS code it enters never reads the
position, and the LLE BIOS returns to the caller through a PC write (an
HLE SWI resumes at LR with no PC write, as mGBA's HLE does). IRQ entry
resets it in the IRQ entry cycles patch that follows (0012).

Needs arm-recomp-core's half: GbaBus::prefetch_reset overrides a virtual
that patch adds, so this patch does not build without it. Leave both out
together for an A/B build.

Tested on macOS arm64 (Apple clang 21) at gbarecomp 5e89943 plus this
series, arm-recomp-core 1f13cdf plus its half:

- gbarecomp's ctest, 52 of 52 (with the gba-tests test ROMs), including
  codegen_tests and the new interpreter_smoke case. Removing the reset
  from runtime_refill_cycles makes codegen_tests fail on its 14 cases
  whose PC write is known only at run time (BX, MOV and ADD to PC, POP and
  LDM with PC).
- A synthetic 4 KiB ROM (no Nintendo data, header logo zero), prefetch1,
  times three loops of 64 stores to EWRAM from the cartridge with WAITCNT
  0x4317, between two timer 0 reads at F/1: the loop above, the same loop
  closed by `bxcc r6`, and a THUMB loop. mGBA 0.10.5: 1424, 1424 and 892
  cycles. gbarecomp 5e89943: 1673, 1673 and 1141, on generated code
  (GBARECOMP_STRICT_STATIC=1, fully static) and on the interpreter
  (GBARECOMP_FORCE_INTERP=1, the BIOS interpreted too). With both halves:
  1424, 1424 and 892 on both backends. The generator and config are in
  tests/repro/ of https://github.com/nvergez/moto-racer-advanced-browser
  (make_rom.py, prefetch1.toml); attach them when filing this patch.
- A commercial game whose race start-up clears 54,459 words of EWRAM with
  the loop above: without the fix its race code arrives one frame later
  than in mGBA. With both halves and 0012, the clear's instruction timeline
  equals mGBA's to the cycle over the 5 frames of the hand-off, and the
  race code arrives on mGBA's frame on the interpreter and on generated
  code.

