+does not reset it: the BIOS code it enters never reads the position, and
+the BIOS's return to the caller is a PC write. Without the reset,
+a loop that runs from the cartridge and stores to RAM (`cmp; strcc [ewram];
+bcc`) kept the position of the opcodes after the loop across the branch back
+and charged its store 8 cycles instead of mGBA's 4 (26 cycles per iteration
+instead of 22, with WAITCNT `4317h`).
